WEBVTT

NOTE Paragraph boundaries measured from synthesis; timing within paragraphs is approximate.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.066
Detection engineering translates
observable behavior into a rule

00:00:04.066 --> 00:00:08.300
that can operate on available telemetry.
Event schemas, collection settings,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.977
sample records, and known behaviors
provide the starting material.

00:00:11.977 --> 00:00:15.766
AI can explain unfamiliar fields,
draft queries, suggest test cases,

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:18.496
and document which log
sources a rule depends on.

00:00:18.496 --> 00:00:22.340
Missing telemetry cannot be repaired
by a more confident explanation.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.283
For a detection of repeated authentication
failures followed by success,

00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:27.925
the details determine meaning.

00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:32.032
Check which fields identify the account
and source, how events are grouped,

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:35.811
what time window applies, and whether
both event types are collected.

00:00:35.811 --> 00:00:39.534
Aggregating across unrelated users
can create a misleading sequence.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:42.820
A model's query draft should make
these assumptions visible.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:45.727
Test representative malicious
and benign activity,

00:00:45.727 --> 00:00:49.447
including administrative behavior
and missing or delayed events.

00:00:49.447 --> 00:00:53.342
Syntax validation establishes
that a query is accepted, not that it

00:00:53.342 --> 00:00:57.818
identifies the intended behavior. Matching
a positive test is a further step.

00:00:57.818 --> 00:01:01.713
Operational usefulness also depends
on false positives, query cost,

00:01:01.713 --> 00:01:05.375
alert context, and whether analysts
can investigate the result.

00:01:05.375 --> 00:01:07.700
These are separate evaluation questions.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.922
In monitoring, models can
summarize suspicious sequences

00:01:10.922 --> 00:01:14.605
and collect relevant asset
or identity context for alert triage.

00:01:14.605 --> 00:01:18.805
The summary remains an interpretation
of events, not a verified incident.

00:01:18.805 --> 00:01:21.912
Preserve links to records
and unresolved alternatives.

00:01:21.912 --> 00:01:25.997
Detection lifecycle work then records
tuning decisions, versions rules,

00:01:25.997 --> 00:01:29.852
monitors performance, and reevaluates
coverage when systems change.

00:01:29.852 --> 00:01:33.765
Writing rules, understanding
telemetry, and managing detections over

00:01:33.765 --> 00:01:37.620
time are related specialties that
AI can support in different ways.
